// The `core/net/tcp` conformance package.
//
// Every case here runs against `core/host/testing`'s `tcp()` double, so the
// suite opens no socket: what it asserts is the module's own arithmetic — that
// `connect` wraps a handle, that `read` takes a prefix, that a closed stream is
// gone — and the log the double keeps of what the code under test did.
//
// The other half is `native::e2e`'s
// `a_native_binary_speaks_over_a_socket_it_dialled`, which is a whole program
// against a real loopback peer. Neither replaces the other: this one says the
// module means what it says, and that one says the runtime is really connected
// to it.
